==========================================================================================
S723 — Erdos 93 (convex, SOLVED) and 98 (general position, OPEN), worked back and forth
==========================================================================================

[93] Altman: convex => >= floor(n/2) distinct distances; regular n-gon is TIGHT and ALL-concyclic
   regular 4-gon: distinct distances = 2  (floor(n/2)=2)  all 4 concyclic => 98-FORBIDDEN for n>=4
   regular 5-gon: distinct distances = 2  (floor(n/2)=2)  all 5 concyclic => 98-FORBIDDEN for n>=4
   regular 6-gon: distinct distances = 3  (floor(n/2)=3)  all 6 concyclic => 98-FORBIDDEN for n>=4
   regular 7-gon: distinct distances = 3  (floor(n/2)=3)  all 7 concyclic => 98-FORBIDDEN for n>=4
   regular 8-gon: distinct distances = 4  (floor(n/2)=4)  all 8 concyclic => 98-FORBIDDEN for n>=4
   regular 9-gon: distinct distances = 4  (floor(n/2)=4)  all 9 concyclic => 98-FORBIDDEN for n>=4
   regular 10-gon: distinct distances = 5  (floor(n/2)=5)  all 10 concyclic => 98-FORBIDDEN for n>=4
   regular 11-gon: distinct distances = 5  (floor(n/2)=5)  all 11 concyclic => 98-FORBIDDEN for n>=4
   regular 12-gon: distinct distances = 6  (floor(n/2)=6)  all 12 concyclic => 98-FORBIDDEN for n>=4

[93->98] hull-size bound: a D-distinct-distance set has convex hull on h <= 2D+1 vertices
   verified h <= 2D+1 on 3000 random integer configs: True
   => few distinct distances FORCES a small convex hull (the regular-polygon ring is the only
      way to a big hull with few distances, and 98 bans it).

[93->98] onion peeling: each convex layer (by 93) has size <= 2D+1 => few distances => many layers
   regular 10-gon (98-forbidden): D=5, #convex layers=1, layer sizes=[10]
   general-position 10-set (no 3 collinear, no 4 concyclic): D=26, layers sizes=[7, 3]
      layer size 7 (convex): distinct distances 18 >= floor/2=3
      layer size 3 (convex): distinct distances 3 >= floor/2=1

[98->93] reverse: no-4-concyclic caps per-vertex distance multiplicity at 3 => every vertex sees
   >= ceil((n-1)/3) distinct distances -- a clean toehold on the OPEN strong-93 (one vertex >= n/2).
   The gap (n-1)/3 -> n/2 is exactly the convex structure 93 exploits but 98 cannot.

==========================================================================================
THE PIVOT: 93's optimizer (regular polygon, 1 concyclic ring, floor(n/2)) = 98's forbidden config.
98 = 93 with the ring banned => must use many thin NON-circular convex layers => candidate route
to superlinearity: bound how few distinct distances many-non-circular-layers can share.
==========================================================================================
